cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  coverage-decay: measuring false-positive suppression in detection
  rule repositories
message: If you use this software or its derived data, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sudaroli
    family-names: Dhananjeyan
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8270-6223
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Bengaluru, India
repository-code: https://github.com/sudaroli1/coverage-decay
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22107282
version: v1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-26'
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Analysis pipeline, derived data and validation record for a study of
  what becomes of false-positive exclusions after they are added to a
  public detection-rule repository. Suppression is detected semantically
  by a deterministic test over the set of predicates a rule holds under
  negation, rather than by structural comparison of rule text. Includes
  the 120-item blinded validation sample and its labels.
keywords:
  - detection engineering
  - security operations
  - alert fatigue
  - Sigma
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - mining software repositories
  - empirical security
